group: Oh
formula: CrC6O6
construction: Fragment orbitals (extended Hückel)
headline: 
note: Energies in Hartree.  Molecular levels are the calculation's own orbital energies in Hartree.  Fragment levels: extended Hueckel, placed by a fitted scale; qualitative.  The fragment orbitals describe the drawn molecular orbitals to 80% - 98% (capture).  Scale: E = 0.71 E(EHT) -0.151 Hartree, fit r = 0.66.  A line is drawn where a fragment orbital makes up at least 10% of an orbital; thicker is more.  14 ligand-internal levels (at least 80% on the ligands, no line to a metal orbital) not drawn.  1 fragment level the scale puts far outside the drawn orbitals not drawn.  6 levels the valence fragment orbitals do not describe (capture below 50%) not drawn.  Symmetry labels computed from the orbitals in Oh (cross-checked against the code's own D2H labels, which agreed on all 199 orbitals both sides could label, and every computed label subduces to match).
